For a {\em potential} $ W: \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{R} $, we denote the corresponding Schr\"odinger operator 
$ \mathcal{H}_W $ acting on $ f\in \mathcal{F}_{\mathbb{N}}^{\sigma} $ as 
\begin{equation*}
	\mathcal{H}_W[f](n)=(-\Delta_{\mathbb{N}})^{\sigma} f(n)- {W(n)}f(n)\,,
\end{equation*}
and its associated energy functional as
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:quadratic}
	\mathcal{Q}_{W}(f,g):=\langle f,\mathcal{H}_W [g]\rangle_{\ell^2(\mathbb{N})}.
\end{equation}
