\noindent
{\bf Abstract:} In this paper we derive two examples of fully-nonlinear symmetry-integrable evolution 
equations with algebraic nonlinearities, namely one class of 3rd-order equations and a 5th-order equation. 
%We show that the so-derived equations can be semi-linearised. 
To achieve this we study the equations' Lie-Bäcklund symmetries and apply multipotentialisations, hodograph transformations and generalised hodograph transformations to map the equations to known semilinear integrable evolution equations. As a result of this, we also obtain interesting symmetry-integrable quasilinear equations of order five and order seven, which we display explicitly.

