\section{Simple $p$-nary butterfly trees}

Next we consider non-binary butterfly permutations. In the $p$-nary case, we consider now 
\begin{equation}
    B^{(m)}_{s,m^n} = \bigotimes_{j=1}^n B_{s,m}^{(m)}
\end{equation}
formed using $B_{s,n}^{(m)} = \langle (1 \ 2 \ \cdots \ m)\rangle$, the cyclic group of order $m$. Note the permutation matrices corresponding to powers of this $m$-cycle form a basis for the $m \times m$ circulant matrices. Previous results on the LIS were $\operatorname{LIS}(\pi_n) \sim \prod_{j=1}^n \max(X_j, m-X_j)$ for $X_j \sim \operatorname{Unif}(\{1,2,\ldots,m\})$, while $\log_2 \operatorname{LDS}(\pi_n) \sim \operatorname{Binom}(n,1 - \frac1m)$, along with corresponding log-normal asymptotics.

