Considering $\P(\Upsilon_n = 1) = \frac1n$ does match $\P(L_n + 1 = 1) = \frac1n$, it stops there, as $\P(\Upsilon_n = 2) = |s(n,2)|/n! \ne H_{n-1}/n$.

