The AGB group is made up of 205 candidates with $14.5<g<15$ mag, leading to a total of 408 candidates in the full sample including PK25. This group shows distinct differences from the first two groups, having larger amplitudes of variability within  each season, and nearly all having evidence of periodicity (346 of 408).
