IllustrisTNG was performed with the moving mesh code \textsc{arepo} \citep{Springel_2010_Arepo}. \textsc{arepo} is characterized by the Voronoi tessellation of a set of discrete mesh generation points that span an unstructured moving mesh on which the magnetohydrodynamic equations are solved \citep{Springel_2010_Arepo}.
This non-uniform structure of the Voronoi mesh makes it difficult to analyze the simulation data, as this means that the $\Delta\xi_l$ are different for different values of $l$.

