	Define $x_t^*:= \arg \min_{x \in [0,1]} f_t(x).$ We make the following assumption in this setting.
	\begin{assumption}\label{asm:a1}
		For all $1 \leq t \leq T$, the function $f_t:[0,1]\rightarrow\mathcal{R^+}$ is $M$-smooth, convex and $f_t(x_t^*)=0$\footnote{This is without loss of generality.}. 
